request.description:
Method: POST
URL: {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/vehicle-jobs/assignment/cancel
Auth: Admin access token with jobs:cancel permission
Replaces the previous POST /api/admin/jobs/cancel, POST .../tickets/{{ticketNo}}/cancel, POST .../tickets/{{ticketNo}}/stalls/{{stallCode}}/cancel, POST .../workers/{{workerCode}}/assignment/cancel, and POST .../tickets/{{ticketNo}}/workers/{{workerCode}}/cancel endpoints — all removed, use this one instead.
Body: TicketNumber required. ReasonCode required, never null — always written to admin_action_logs, whichever scope below is resolved; ReasonText optional. TicketNo/BoothCode/WorkerCode optional (send null or omit). Scope is decided purely by which of TicketNo/BoothCode/WorkerCode are present:
TicketNumber alone -> cancel the whole vehicle job (all workers requeued to front of queue). Only ever cascades to Business Tickets/Booths that are not already COMPLETED/CANCELLED — a booth/market that already finished stays untouched. Rejects 409 VehicleJobClosed if the vehicle is already COMPLETED or CANCELLED (row-locked and re-checked in the same transaction as the cancel, so this also catches a vehicle a concurrent vendor confirmation just closed).
+ TicketNo -> cancel that one Business Ticket (cascades to every non-terminal booth under it). Rejects 409 MarketJobAlreadyClosed / MarketJobAlreadySubmitted. After cancelling, the parent vehicle job's status is recalculated in the same transaction (same centralized lifecycle vendor confirmation uses) — it becomes COMPLETED if another Business Ticket already completed, CANCELLED if every Business Ticket ended up cancelled, or stays as-is if other Business Tickets are still active.
+ TicketNo + BoothCode -> cancel that one Booth only, roster untouched. Rejects 409 StallJobAlreadyClosed / StallJobAlreadySubmitted. After cancelling, the parent Business Ticket and vehicle job status are recalculated in the same transaction (same centralized lifecycle vendor confirmation uses) — e.g. if this was the last non-terminal booth and a sibling booth already completed, the Business Ticket finalizes financials and becomes COMPLETED, and the vehicle job follows the same rule as above.
+ WorkerCode (no TicketNo) -> cancel that one worker's assignment for the whole vehicle job.
+ TicketNo + WorkerCode (no BoothCode) -> remove that one worker from that one Business Ticket's roster only, worker stays checked in on the truck.
+ TicketNo + BoothCode + WorkerCode together -> remove that one worker from just that one Booth's payout divisor only (does not touch the worker's roster status at all — they stay WORKING on the rest of the Business Ticket and keep working any other booth in it). Allowed until that booth has ever been submitted (DELIVERED or REJECT), same as full Booth cancellation. Rejects 404 TicketWorkerNotFound if the worker is not an active member of the ticket, 409 StallJobAlreadyClosed/StallJobAlreadySubmitted for the booth's own state, or 409 WorkerAlreadyExcludedFromBooth if already removed from this booth.
ReasonCode/ReasonText traceability: GET .../vehicle-jobs/history Workers[].Cancellation and GET .../vehicle-jobs/history/daily-worker-income Cancellation both read ReasonCode/ReasonText/CancelledByType/CancelledByName from whichever admin_action_logs row actually caused that worker/ticket_no to end up cancelled — including indirectly: a worker/ticket_no cancelled as a side effect of a whole-vehicle cancel (TicketNumber alone) falls back to that VEHICLE_JOB_CANCELLED log, and a ticket_no cancelled as a side effect of its last Booth being cancelled falls back to that STALL_JOB_CANCELLED log, so the Reason you send here always surfaces on those two GET endpoints no matter which scope actually triggered the cancellation.
Examples:
Whole vehicle: { "TicketNumber": "{{ticketNumber}}", "ReasonCode": "ADMIN_CANCEL", "ReasonText": "Admin cancelled this job." }
One Business Ticket: { "TicketNumber": "{{ticketNumber}}", "TicketNo": "{{ticketNo}}", "ReasonCode": "ADMIN_CANCEL", "ReasonText": "Cancelled by admin." }
One Booth: { "TicketNumber": "{{ticketNumber}}", "TicketNo": "{{ticketNo}}", "BoothCode": "{{boothCode}}", "ReasonCode": "ADMIN_CANCEL", "ReasonText": "Cancelled by admin." }
One worker, whole vehicle: { "TicketNumber": "{{ticketNumber}}", "WorkerCode": "{{workerCode}}", "ReasonCode": "ADMIN_CANCEL", "ReasonText": "Cancel this worker assignment." }
One worker, one Business Ticket: { "TicketNumber": "{{ticketNumber}}", "TicketNo": "{{ticketNo}}", "WorkerCode": "{{workerCode}}", "ReasonCode": "ADMIN_CANCEL", "ReasonText": "Vendor requested a different worker for this ticket only." }
One worker, one Booth: { "TicketNumber": "{{ticketNumber}}", "TicketNo": "{{ticketNo}}", "BoothCode": "{{boothCode}}", "WorkerCode": "{{workerCode}}", "ReasonCode": "ADMIN_CANCEL", "ReasonText": "Worker was reassigned to a different booth." }

